# RIO — AI Voice Call Assistant

RIO is a voice-to-voice AI assistant. You speak, RIO listens, thinks with the Groq API, and answers out loud — with an animated avatar that shows whether RIO is **idle, listening, thinking or speaking**.

## Features
- Phone-style call screen: Start Call / End Call, call timer, mic and speaker status
- Animated CSS avatar (glow rings, listening mic pulse, thinking orbit, speaking waves)
- Speech-to-text with Groq Whisper, replies from a Groq chat model, natural neural text-to-speech
- Short, conversational answers and per-session memory (with a Clear Conversation button)
- Mute mic / mute speaker, replay last answer, friendly error messages
- API key stored in Streamlit Secrets, never in the code

## How it works
`Microphone → st.audio_input → Groq Whisper → Groq chat (openai/gpt-oss-20b) → edge-tts (gTTS fallback) → Speaker`

**Limitation:** Streamlit cannot stream microphone audio continuously, so RIO is *turn-based push-to-talk*: press the mic, speak, press stop, hear RIO's answer, repeat. This also guarantees RIO's own voice is never fed back into speech recognition. Use headphones for the best experience.

## Tech stack
Python, Streamlit, Groq SDK (chat + Whisper), edge-tts, gTTS.

## Installation
```bash
git clone YOUR_GITHUB_REPOSITORY_URL
cd RIO-AI-Voice-Assistant
python -m venv .venv && source .venv/bin/activate   # Windows: .venv\Scripts\activate
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

## Groq API setup
1. Create a free key at https://console.groq.com/keys
2. Copy `.streamlit/secrets.toml.example` to `.streamlit/secrets.toml` and paste your key:
```toml
GROQ_API_KEY = "gsk_..."
```
`secrets.toml` is git-ignored. Never commit it.

## Run locally
```bash
streamlit run app.py
```
Allow microphone access when the browser asks (`localhost` is allowed over HTTP).

## Change the model
Edit the configuration block at the top of `app.py` (`GROQ_MODEL`, `STT_MODELS`, `TTS_VOICE`). Groq retires models regularly — check https://console.groq.com/docs/deprecations. (`llama-3.1-8b-instant` was shut down for free/developer tiers on 16 Aug 2026.)

